{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And the feast of the harvest — [this is the festival of Shavuot, on which they bring] the offerings written in the passage of bull or sheep, and the two loaves, which are a new meal-offering." "The first-fruits of your labors — to permit new grain in the sanctuary." "And the feast of ingathering — the festival of Sukkot, at the time of ingathering, when the threshing-floors are full of grain and the vats of new wine and oil, and Scripture commanded to dwell in booths as a remembrance, for in the wilderness they dwelt in tents and had no land and no grain, new wine, or oil. You see that the three festivals all depend on the produce of the land: aviv; harvest; ingathering."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:48.896425342Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}